;; Regulatory source register for kotoba-lang/robotics — the safety-governor
;; library that refuses unsafe robot actuation before it reaches hardware.
;;
;; README.md says the governor refuses actions a robot should not take; until
;; this file existed there was no list of the authorities a safety
;; classification could be traced to. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository — extend the table, never invent an id or a
;; URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljk`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it.
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be:
;;                   laws.e-gov.go.jp is a single-page app that answers
;;                   HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>, renders "not found"
;;                   client-side, and therefore cannot tell a real citation
;;                   from an invented one.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; WHY THIS DOMAIN CITES THE INDUSTRIAL-SAFETY ACT AND NOT A ROBOT-SPECIFIC
;; STATUTE NAMED AFTER ROBOTS. There is no Japanese statute bearing the word
;; robot in its title; industrial-robot safety is regulated as "機械" (machinery)
;; under 労働安全衛生法 and its subordinate instruments. 労働安全衛生法施行令 is the
;; enforcement order; the operator-level duties for industrial robots sit in
;; 労働安全衛生規則 articles 150 の 3–151 (第9節 産業用ロボット). The two MHLW pages
;; cited here are the ministry's own statement of exactly that: the notice
;; carrying the enforcement guidance for 安衛則第150条の4 cites the article in
;; its title, and the workplace-safety index names the cooperative-robot
;; clarification. JIS (日本産業標準調査会) is the standards body whose B8433
;; series is the Japanese adoption of ISO 10218 — the machine-safety standard
;; the guidance names — so its front page is the standards half of the
;; register.
;;
;; THE HOSTS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT. The
;; :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path that
;; does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every host in
;; the register and fails if the answer has changed. A dated note saying
;; "measured to refuse correctly" degrades into a constant the moment it is
;; written; a declaration the run re-measures cannot.
;;
;; MEASURED 2026-09-09: BOTH www.mhlw.go.jp and www.jisc.go.jp answer **404**,
;; not 403 harder and not a soft-404, for a path that does not exist — a real
;; "このページは存在しません" body served at the requested URL with its own
;; stable title. Neither host serves a WAF challenge (no awswaf markers in any
;; body seen). Both redirect **http -> https** without declaring a redirect,
;; which is what makes the verifier's unexpected-redirect self-test discriminate.
;;
;; ISO org (iso.org) is deliberately NOT cited: measured 2026-09-09 it answers
;; the automated client a Cloudflare challenge ("Just a moment...", HTTP 403).
;; ISO 10218 is described by the two MHLW pages (which name it) and by the JIS
;; standards index; the register establishes the authorities that answer, and
;; :coverage/not-covered says the ISO pages themselves were not-cited, not
;; absent.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in a robot-safety register. Claims stop
;; at the level actually checked — law identity, and for the pages the title,
;; the URL, the charset and the strings read on 2026-09-09. No article text
;; and no standard's content is asserted, because none was read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run.

 {:source/id "host.www-mhlw-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.mhlw.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "厚生労働省. For a path that does not exist answers 404 with a
                42503-byte お探しのページが見つかりません。 page served at the
                requested URL. Redirects http rules to https. No WAF challenge
                markers observed in any response."}

 {:source/id "host.www-jisc-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.jisc.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "日本産業標準調査会 (JISC), the agency administering JIS.
                For a path that does not exist answers 404 with a 1166-byte
                ファイルが見つかりません page. Redirects http rules to https,
                and serves its front page and search form with the exact
                title recorded below. No WAF challenge markers observed."}

